cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Argus in your research, please cite the technical report."
title: "Argus: A General-Purpose Agentic Runtime for Long-Horizon Reasoning"
abstract: >-
  Argus is a persistent agentic runtime organized around Manager, Planner,
  Engineer and Reviewer roles over bounded missions and durable project state.
  A change of direction must be evidence-backed, admitted through a
  role-separated gate, and recorded with its justification, so that verified
  pivoting is distinguishable from rationalized failure. Reviewer-gated
  outcomes feed fixed-model runtime self-evolution.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Argus Team"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lbx154/Argus"
url: "https://argusbot.cn/"
license: MIT
year: 2026
keywords:
  - agentic runtime
  - long-horizon reasoning
  - verified pivoting
  - runtime self-evolution
  - autonomous research
